================================================================================================
PATH A — the theorem's three claims, measured
================================================================================================

  (1) CIRCUITS PER EPOCH, and (3) DEPTH. Claim: ~1.5G circuits,
      constant in M; depth = ansatz depth + O(1).

    N reps    M  G   L  n/blk  circ/ep qpe  circ/ep dir   1.5G  anz depth   d qpe   d dir
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    4    1   16  3   4      4            4           12    4.5          3     274      10
    4    2   24  3   6      4            6           18    4.5          5     277      14
    4    3   32  3   8      4            8           24    4.5          7     280      18
    6    1   24  3   4      6            4           12    4.5          5     466      12
    6    2   36  3   6      6            6           18    4.5          7     469      16
    8    1   32  3   4      8            4           12    4.5          7     658      14

  L is the number of blocks _layers() produces. If L tracks M/N rather
  than sitting near 1.5, claim (1)'s constant describes T10's optimal
  blocking, which v5 does not implement.

  (2) SHOT SCALING. Claim eps ~ sqrt(M/(R^2 S)), so L2 error of the
      sensed gradient against the EXACT R-smoothed target should fall
      as 1/sqrt(S). Direct mode, block 0, 4 repeats.

    N reps    M   n   shots    L2 err  err*sqrt(S)  rel err
  -------------------------------------------------------
    4    1   16   4     256   0.42819        6.851   0.3932
    4    1   16   4    1024   0.22584        7.227   0.2074
    4    1   16   4    4096   0.10279        6.578   0.0944
    4    1   16   4   16384   0.08220       10.521   0.0755
  .......................................................
    4    2   24   4     256   0.47028        7.525   0.5036
    4    2   24   4    1024   0.23595        7.550   0.2527
    4    2   24   4    4096   0.11475        7.344   0.1229
    4    2   24   4   16384   0.07827       10.019   0.0838
  .......................................................
    6    1   24   6     256   0.98495       15.759   0.4453
    6    1   24   6    1024   0.40323       12.903   0.1823
    6    1   24   6    4096   0.22787       14.584   0.1030
    6    1   24   6   16384   0.14756       18.888   0.0667
  .......................................................

  err*sqrt(S) flat down a column confirms the 1/sqrt(S) half of claim (2).
  Comparing that constant ACROSS blocks of different width tests the
  sqrt(M) half - it should grow with n, since T4 gives
  Var(g_i) = (1/S)[a + b(n-1)].
